THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL - use-railway

This directory started as somebody else's work and has been edited here. It is
not RichOS-authored and it is not covered by this repository's AGPL.

  Source     https://github.com/railwayapp/railway-skills
  Skill      plugins/railway/skills/use-railway
  Revision   1b59fd592cd4413f3c325f139bf3f3afa99ee095 (2026-07-09), the revision
             that declares skill version 1.3.5 - the version the bundled copy
             declares in its own text
  Terms      MIT, from the upstream LICENSE file at that revision, reproduced
             verbatim below

HOW THE REVISION WAS PINNED. All thirty upstream revisions of the skill were
fetched and compared on 2026-09-04. This one is the closest: 24 differing lines
out of roughly 600, against 34 for upstream's current main and 38 for the next
nearest. It is also the revision whose declared version matches the bundled
copy's, and it is five days older than the merge recorded in this project's
source repository at 2026-07-14.

THE DIFFERENCES, so that "modified" means something specific here.
  - Two hyphens and one semicolon replaced by em dashes in one paragraph on
    context resolution.
  - One added command line: railway service status --all --json.
  - One word: "the exact command the user must run" became "should run".
  - One dropped step and the renumbering it forced: upstream's first step,
    which routes deploy-from-cwd and signup-from-cwd straight to railway up,
    is absent here, and the sub-bullets under the steps that remain are
    indented four spaces rather than three.

MIT does not require any of that to be disclosed. It is disclosed because
docs/legal/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md records this skill as modified, and a reader
who wants to know what was modified should not have to diff it themselves.

